      <p class="archived-comment-meta"><strong>jkaljundi</strong> &middot; <time datetime="2016-11-25T14:30:19Z">November 25, 2016</time></p>
      <div class="archived-comment-body"><p>Good stuff. While I'm biased towards our product, Weekdone, which does exactly weekly status updates (<a href="https://weekdone.com/)" rel="nofollow ugc noopener" target="_blank">https://weekdone.com/)</a> many things in regard to the process and value sounded the same we see many teams do.</p><p>The biggest complaint we hear from employees is that their leaders and managers don't share anything with them. Leaders want people to give status updates, but never do it themselves. It then rarely works. If leaders participate as almost equals the results are much better. Communication after all is 2-way.</p><p>Have you tried writing your daily updates into the doc right away? Wouldn't many people prefer that, as opposed to find time to read a 2-page doc? What we've seen is many people nowadays prefer smaller chunks of information in shorter intervals, and more gets read that way. Of course, it can be also more distracting.</p><p>Anyway thanks for showing a good example of other leaders!</p></div>
    </li>
